// Syncthing ignore file for the Everlight workspace.
// Phone <-> AceMagician PC bidirectional sync.
//
// PRINCIPLE: git handles version-controlled code/doctrine (it flows through
// GitHub). Syncthing handles the UNTRACKED data. Anything git already syncs
// is excluded here to avoid double-sync conflicts.
//
// Lines starting with // are comments. (?d) = delete if it becomes ignored.

// ---- git internals: git syncs these through GitHub, never Syncthing ----
.git
**/.git
.gitignore

// ---- build artifacts + dependency trees (regenerable, huge, churny) ----
node_modules
**/node_modules
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
.turbo
.parcel-cache
*.egg-info

// ---- caches + ephemeral state ----
.cache
**/.cache
*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.sync_conflicts
~syncthing~*

// ---- the Syncthing config dir itself (never sync your own config) ----
_logs/syncthing_config

// ---- venvs + large installed packages (machine-specific binaries) ----
// Open WebUI etc. -- each machine installs its own; .so files are arch-specific
open_webui_pkgs
**/open_webui_pkgs
open_webui_venv
**/open_webui_venv
*.venv
venv

// ---- proot / android cruft if it ever leaks in ----
.android
.Xauthority

// ---- worktrees: separate git working trees, git owns these ----
// (kept as a phone-side sibling; not part of the synced workspace)

// NOTE: everything NOT matched above DOES sync. That includes:
//   _logs/ (except syncthing_config), owner_downloads/, Blinko DB,
//   deal_execution.sqlite, reports, parsed leads, intel DBs, etc.
//   -- exactly the untracked data that makes the PC "as smart as the phone."
